    'That night,','Adam went up to the roof.','The air was a little cold,','and the neighborhood was quiet after the long Friday.','He sat on an old chair,','and placed the notebook on his lap.','He reopened the first page where he had written his salary plan.','It contained many crossed-out items,','numbers that had changed,','and things he had not bought.','He looked at the list and laughed.','Before receiving the salary,','he had thought his first salary would solve everything.','He imagined he would buy everything he wanted,','give money to his family,','and still have plenty left.','But when he received it,','he understood that money was not magic.','A person had to choose.','What was most important?','What could wait?','What needed to be saved?','And what could he help with?','He thought again about the gifts.','The perfume that made his mother smile when she smelled it.','The wallet his father began using that same day.','And the mug Nour was drinking from,','although she kept saying she wanted headphones.','He also thought about the envelope he gave the household,','and the money his mother returned inside his bag.','His first salary was not large.','It did not cover everything he wanted.','But it made him feel something he had not felt in a long time.','That he was now able to help.','That he now had responsibility.','And that his effort had value,','even if the amount was modest.','He closed the notebook,','and looked at the sky.','The lights in the homes around him went out one after another.','From below,','he heard his mother calling him to come down.','He stood up,','and placed the notebook under his arm.','Before going down,','he told himself:','“Next month,','I want to be better.”','He did not mean only at work.','He meant being better at how he worked hard,','how he spent,','how he saved,','and how he appreciated what he had.','He went down to the house,','and closed the roof door behind him.','His first salary remained stored in his memory,','not because of how much it was.','But because it was the first time he felt he had begun taking part of his life into his own hands.','The end.'
