const yomAilaPageTranslations = [
`From Thursday evening, Umm Adam was already preparing for Friday.

There was no major occasion, no holiday, and nobody was returning from abroad. But Adam’s grandmother wanted to invite her sons and daughters for lunch, and that alone was enough to make the day begin early.

Before Adam went to bed, his mother told him not to stay up too late because they needed to leave for his grandmother’s home before noon. Adam nodded and said he would sleep early. Naturally, he did not.

He spent time on his phone, then opened his laptop and kept watching one thing after another. When he checked the time, it was almost half past one. He told himself that perhaps he could wake up at ten.

But at eight in the morning, his mother’s voice from the living room woke him. She was calling for Nour and saying it was getting late, although Adam thought eight o’clock was still far too early.

He opened his eyes and tried to go back to sleep. A minute later, he heard his bedroom door opening. His mother stood in the doorway and said, “Come on, Adam, get up. We need to stop at the market before we go.”

He closed his eyes again. “Mum, it’s still early.”

She replied that she knew that line, and that if she left him for another half hour, it would be noon while he was still in bed.

After she left, Adam remained sitting on the bed for a few seconds, his hair disheveled and his face still half asleep. The smell of coffee reached his room from the kitchen. From the living room, he could hear Nour searching for something she had lost and his father saying that the same thing happened every Friday.

Adam finally stood up. He knew it would be a long day. He also knew that a family day did not begin when they reached his grandmother’s home. It began the moment his mother opened his bedroom door and said, “Come on, get up.”`,
  '', '', '', '', '', '', '', '', ''
];
