yomAilaPageTranslations[1] = `After breakfast, Adam went to the market with his mother. His father said he would wait at home because whenever Umm Adam entered the market, nobody knew when she would come out. His mother took offense and insisted that she knew exactly what she needed. Adam said nothing. Experience had taught him that the words “I know what I need” had nothing to do with how long the trip would take.

Their first stop was the vegetable shop. His mother ordered tomatoes, cucumbers, parsley, and mint. Then she remembered that his grandmother had asked for lemons, so she added a bag of those as well. Adam followed behind her carrying the bags.

They passed the sweet shop, and she stopped. Adam looked at her. “Didn’t you say Grandma had made dessert?” His mother said she knew, but it would not be right to arrive empty-handed. Adam looked at all the bags he was carrying. It was difficult to believe that their hands were empty.

After the sweet shop, they stopped at the grocery store. Then his mother remembered that she wanted to buy coffee for his grandmother. After the coffee, she noticed some tissues at a good price and bought several packets. Adam kept taking one bag after another.

By the end of the trip, he was carrying bags in both hands with the box of sweets tucked beneath his arm. He looked at his mother and said, “Mum, are we going to lunch, or are we opening a grocery store?” She laughed and told him to stop talking and keep walking.

On the way home, the market was crowded. Vendors called from every direction, and the smells of bread and spices blended together. Although Adam was tired from carrying the bags, he liked the atmosphere.

Nearly every Friday, the market looked the same: people in a hurry, women comparing prices, children asking their parents for sweets, and men standing beside the shops discussing everything except shopping.

When they returned home, his father was dressed and ready. He looked at Adam entering beneath the load of bags, smiled, and said, “Didn’t she tell you she knew what she needed?” Umm Adam gave him a look that immediately silenced him. Adam laughed. The day was only beginning.`;
