akhirBasClauseTranslations[3] = ['Adam quickly put on his jacket.','Samer’s mother tried to give him a bag with some food to take home,','but Adam told her he was in a hurry.','Samer went out with him.','The stop was about a ten-minute walk away.','They walked quickly,','then began to run a little.','The street was quieter than before.','Most shops were still open,','but there were fewer people around.','As they approached the stop,','they saw a white shared taxi pulling away.','Samer raised his hand.','He shouted:','“Wait!','Adam ran.','But the shared taxi kept going.','A few seconds later,','it disappeared at the end of the street.','Adam stopped,','with his hands on his knees,','catching his breath.','Samer stopped beside him.','“Maybe that wasn’t the last one.','Adam looked at him.','“Didn’t you say the last one leaves at eight thirty?','Samer told him it was approximately eight thirty.','Adam did not like the word “approximately” at that moment.','They waited at the stop.','An older man was standing nearby.','Samer asked whether any shared taxis were still going toward Adam’s area.','The man thought for a moment.','He said the one that had just passed might have been the last direct one.','But Adam could go to another area,','and find another shared taxi from there.','Adam opened the map on his phone.','The route was not clear to him.','Samer said Adam could come back and sleep at their home,','then return home in the morning.','Adam shook his head.','He had work the next day.','His clothes were at home.','And so was his phone charger.','He checked the battery percentage.','Twenty-one percent.','He said:','“No,','I want to go home.','Ten minutes later,','a shared taxi arrived heading toward a nearby area.','Samer asked the driver if Adam could find transportation home from there.','The driver said:','“God willing, you’ll find something.','Adam did not like the words “God willing” this time either.','But he had no better option.','He got in.','Samer stood by the shared taxi’s door.','He told him:','“Message me as soon as you arrive.','Adam nodded.','The shared taxi pulled away.','As he watched Samer through the window,','he sensed that the journey home would be much longer than he had expected.'];
akhirBasPageTranslations[3] = akhirBasClauseTranslations[3].join(' ');

akhirBasClauseTranslations[4] = ['Adam sat in the back of the shared taxi.','There were four other passengers.','An older man.','A young man wearing work clothes.','And a woman with her little daughter.','The shared taxi moved through streets Adam did not know well.','In daylight,','the area might have seemed ordinary.','But at night,','everything looked different.','Half the shops were closed.','There were fewer lights.','And unfamiliar streets seemed longer.','He opened his phone,','and messaged his mother:','“I’m a little late.','I’m on my way.','A few seconds later,','his phone rang.','His mother.','He answered.','Her first question was:','“Where are you?','Adam did not want to tell her that he did not know exactly where he was.','He said he had found a ride,','and would change shared taxis somewhere else.','His mother was silent for a moment.','Then she said:','“Take care of yourself,','and keep me updated.','He ended the call.','About twenty minutes later,','the driver announced that they had reached the end of the route.','Adam got out.','He looked around.','He had expected to find a large stop or shared taxis waiting.','But there were only a few cars,','an open shop,','and two men standing on the sidewalk.','He asked the driver:','“Where can I find a shared taxi to…?','He said the name of his area.','The driver pointed to a street on the other side.','“Walk that way,','by the traffic light.','You might find one.','Adam looked toward the traffic light.','It was about five minutes away.','He thanked him,','and walked on.','When he arrived,','he found a man standing at the door of a grocery store.','He asked him about the shared taxis.','The man said:','“They’ve most likely finished for the night.','Adam’s stomach dropped.','“All of them?','The man said one might still pass,','but there was no guarantee.','Adam checked the time.','It was nine thirty-five.','Then he checked the battery.','Fourteen percent.','He stood on the sidewalk.','For the first time since the journey began,','he started to understand that this was more than a delay.','He truly might have missed the last bus.'];
akhirBasPageTranslations[4] = akhirBasClauseTranslations[4].join(' ');

akhirBasClauseTranslations[5] = ['Ten minutes passed.','Nothing.','Every time a car approached,','Adam raised his head.','But it was either a private car,','or a shared taxi going somewhere else.','The night air began to turn cold.','Adam zipped up his jacket,','and put his hands in his pockets.','He regretted every extra half hour he had spent at Samer’s.','At seven o’clock,','he could have gone home.','At seven thirty,','he still could have.','Even at eight,','he might have caught it.','But every time he said:','“Just a little longer.','And now,','all those little delays had added up,','leaving him in an unfamiliar street at a quarter to ten.','His phone rang.','Samer.','He answered.','Samer asked whether he had arrived.','Adam gave a joyless laugh.','He told him he was still waiting for a shared taxi.','Samer fell silent.','Then he said:','“Come back to my place.','Adam asked how he was supposed to return,','when he had no transportation in the first place.','Samer said he might come and pick him up in his friend’s car.','At first, Adam refused.','He did not want to inconvenience anyone.','But Samer asked him:','“Where exactly are you?','Adam opened the map.','He sent him his location.','A minute later,','Samer called again.','He said his friend was far away,','and they would need more than half an hour to reach him.','Adam looked at the street.','He said:','“Wait a little.','Maybe I’ll find something.','Samer was not convinced.','Before ending the call,','he told Adam not to let his phone die.','Adam checked the battery.','Nine percent.','He entered the grocery store.','He asked the owner if he had a charger.','The man had an old charger,','and agreed to let Adam charge his phone for a while.','Adam stood beside the refrigerator,','with his phone plugged into a socket on the wall.','He bought a bottle of water,','and sat on a plastic chair outside the shop.','The grocery-store owner was a man in his sixties.','He asked Adam where he had come from.','Adam briefly told him the story.','The man laughed.','“That’s what happens to someone who says: I’ll go home in a little while.','Adam laughed.','He felt that everyone had joined forces against him that day.'];
akhirBasPageTranslations[5] = akhirBasClauseTranslations[5].join(' ');

akhirBasClauseTranslations[6] = ['At around ten fifteen,','Adam was still sitting outside the grocery store.','His battery had reached twenty-five percent.','He told himself that at least this was something good.','He was almost convinced that he should call Samer and let him come pick him up.','But before he took out his phone,','the grocery-store owner stood up.','He pointed at a shared taxi approaching from the end of the street.','“Ask that one.','Adam quickly stood up.','He unplugged the charger from his phone,','and ran toward the street.','He raised his hand.','The shared taxi stopped.','He opened the door,','and asked the driver about his area.','The driver shook his head.','“I’m not going there.','Adam felt disappointed.','But the driver continued:','“I pass nearby.','I can drop you at the roundabout,','and from there you might find a taxi,','or walk part of the way.','Adam asked how far the roundabout was from his home.','The driver thought.','“On foot?','Maybe half an hour…','thirty-five minutes.','Adam did not need to think.','He got in.','Before the shared taxi moved,','he turned toward the grocery-store owner and raised his hand.','“Thank you.','The man replied:','“May God get you home safely.','The shared taxi moved off.','There were three other men inside besides Adam.','They all appeared to be returning from work.','Nobody was talking.','The driver had the radio playing quietly.','Adam rested his head against the window.','For the first time in an hour,','he felt that he was truly heading toward home.','He messaged his mother:','“I found a shared taxi.','I’m heading back now.','She replied quickly:','“Thank God.','Let me know when you get out.','He messaged Samer too.','Samer replied:','“Next time I tell you it’s the last bus,','believe me.','Adam smiled.','He put the phone in his pocket.','And thought that the day was still not over.','Because after getting out of this shared taxi,','he still faced the longest half-hour walk he had taken in years.'];
akhirBasPageTranslations[6] = akhirBasClauseTranslations[6].join(' ');

akhirBasClauseTranslations[7] = ['Adam got out at the roundabout at ten to eleven.','The street was not completely empty,','but it was much quieter than during the day.','A few taxis passed.','He stopped one,','and asked the fare.','The driver named a price that made Adam stare at him for a few seconds.','It was far higher than the usual transportation fare.','He thanked him,','and let him drive away.','Adam had money.','But home was not that far away.','He opened the map.','Walking time: thirty-three minutes.','He took a breath.','And began walking.','At first,','he walked quickly.','He just wanted to arrive and be done with it.','After ten minutes,','he slowed down a little.','His legs were tired from the whole day.','And his shoes,','which were comfortable at work,','were not comfortable for a half-hour walk.','He passed a bakery that was about to close.','The man at the door was collecting the bread crates.','Then he passed a small coffee shop,','where a few men sat playing backgammon.','The clatter of the pieces was clear in the quiet street.','Every place looked different from the daytime.','During the day,','Adam was always in a hurry.','He checked the time.','He waited for a shared taxi.','He thought about work.','But now,','there was nothing except the road.','He walked on.','After fifteen minutes,','his phone rang.','His father.','He answered.','His father asked where he had reached.','Adam told him he had left the shared taxi,','and was walking home.','His father was silent for a second.','“You’re walking?','Why didn’t you take a taxi?','Adam said the distance was short.','His father asked where he was.','When Adam told him,','he replied:','“Stay where you are.','I’m coming to get you.','Adam objected.','He said he was nearly home.','His father did not argue.','“Stay where you are.','And he hung up.','Adam stopped at the side of the street.','He looked at his phone.','Then he laughed to himself.','All day long,','he had insisted on doing everything by himself.','And now,','at the end of the day,','his father was leaving home to collect him just as he had when Adam was little.'];
akhirBasPageTranslations[7] = akhirBasClauseTranslations[7].join(' ');

akhirBasClauseTranslations[8] = ['About ten minutes later,','Adam saw his father’s car approaching.','He stood at the side of the street,','and raised his hand.','His father stopped beside him.','Adam opened the door,','and got in.','As soon as he sat down,','he realized how tired his legs were.','At first, his father said nothing.','The car started moving.','A minute later,','he asked him:','“What happened to you?','Adam told him the story.','Starting from when he finished work late.','Then went to Samer’s.','Then missed the last shared taxi.','And how he had moved from one area to another.','His father kept listening without interrupting.','When Adam finished,','his father said:','“So you could have left Samer’s early from the start.','Adam nodded.','“Yes.','“And Samer told you the last shared taxi leaves early?','“Yes.','“And you still stayed?','Adam looked out the window.','“Yes.','His father fell silent.','Adam waited for the lecture.','But it did not come.','A little later,','his father laughed.','Adam turned toward him.','“What?','His father told him the same thing had happened to him when he was about Adam’s age.','He had been at a friend’s home,','missed the last transportation,','and had to walk for more than an hour.','Adam’s grandfather had been angry with him,','because back then there were no phones to reassure the family.','Adam looked at his father.','“What did Grandpa do?','His father laughed.','“The next day he made me walk to work so I would learn.','Adam laughed.','“You’re not going to do that,','right?','His father did not answer directly.','He said:','“We’ll see in the morning.','Adam knew he was joking.','After that, a comfortable silence settled inside the car.','The streets passed beside them.','This time,','Adam was not worried about where he would get out.','Or whether he would find a shared taxi.','He was sitting beside his father,','and knew the road led directly home.','As they approached the neighborhood,','his father said:','“Next time,','don’t plan your time down to the final minute.','Adam nodded.','“I’ve learned.','His father looked at him.','“Good.','Because I’m not coming out every time to collect you from the streets.','Adam laughed.','He knew that if it happened again,','his father would still come and get him.','But it was better not to test that.'];
akhirBasPageTranslations[8] = akhirBasClauseTranslations[8].join(' ');

akhirBasClauseTranslations[9] = ['They reached home at around eleven thirty.','As soon as Adam opened the door,','he found his mother sitting in the living room.','The television was on,','but it was clear that she had not been watching it.','The moment she saw Adam,','she stood up.','“Thank God you’re safe.','Adam smiled.','“God keep you safe.','His mother told him she had kept checking her phone every five minutes,','and that next time, if he was going to be late, he should tell her early.','Adam said even he had not known he would be this late.','Nour came out of her room.','She was wearing pajamas,','and her hair was tied back.','She looked at Adam.','“I heard you got lost.','Adam did not like the word “lost.”','“I wasn’t lost.','There just wasn’t any transportation.','Nour smiled.','“So you got lost in the transportation system.','His father laughed while placing the keys on the table.','Adam did not argue.','He was too tired to defend his dignity.','He entered the kitchen.','His mother had left him a plate of food,','even though he had told her from the start not to wait for him for dinner.','She asked:','“Did you eat at Samer’s?','Adam nodded.','“Yes.','His mother covered the plate and put it in the refrigerator.','“You can eat it tomorrow.','Before entering his room,','Adam opened his phone.','There was a message from Samer:','“Did you arrive?','He replied:','“Yes,','just now.','Samer messaged him:','“Next time you go home at seven.','Adam wrote:','“Next time, you come to my place.','Samer sent a laughing emoji.','Adam put his phone on the charger,','and changed his clothes.','He sat on the bed.','The day had begun at six thirty in the morning.','Work.','A delay.','A visit.','A shared taxi.','A stop.','Waiting.','A grocery store.','Another shared taxi.','Walking.','And finally,','his father’s car.','He thought about how a short trip could turn into a whole story simply because someone said:','“Just a little longer.','Then he remembered the grocery-store owner.','And the driver who dropped him nearby.','And Samer, who had been ready to come get him.','And his father, who had left home in the middle of the night so Adam would not keep walking.','The day had been exhausting.','But Adam felt there was something good within all that exhaustion too.','A person might land in trouble through his own mistake.','But that did not mean he would be left alone.','He stretched out on the bed,','and reached to turn off the light.','Before sleeping,','he set the alarm.','Six thirty.','He checked the time.','He had less than seven hours of sleep left.','He sighed.','He told himself:','“Tomorrow I’m going straight home from work.','He turned off the light.','A few minutes later,','he fell asleep.','This time there was no last bus for him to catch.','But there was an alarm that would ring sooner than he wanted.'];
akhirBasPageTranslations[9] = akhirBasClauseTranslations[9].join(' ');

