yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[0] = ['On Saturday morning,','Adam woke to the sound of his mother knocking on his bedroom door.','He did not open his eyes right away.','He was still tired from the workweek,','and planned to stay asleep until noon.','Since Friday night,','he had kept his phone on silent so nobody would wake him.','But he had forgotten one thing.','His mother did not need a phone to wake him.','The knocking came again.','“Adam!','He opened his eyes and checked the time.','It was nine fifteen.','He answered in a half-asleep voice:','“What is it,','Mom?','His mother called from behind the door:','“Get up,','we need to go to the market.','Adam closed his eyes again.','The market was the last place he wanted to visit on his day off.','He said:','“You and Nour go.','The answer came quickly:','“Nour has studying to do.','From his mother’s tone, Adam knew the matter was settled.','He sat up on the bed,','and rubbed his face with his hands.','Half an hour later,','he was sitting at the breakfast table,','with a glass of tea in front of him.','His mother held a small piece of paper,','checking what she needed to buy.','Adam looked at the paper.','The list was longer than he had expected.','Tomatoes.','Cucumbers.','Potatoes.','Onions.','Eggplants.','Peppers.','Fruit.','Rice.','Sugar.','Oil.','Cleaning supplies.','And several more things written in small handwriting underneath.','Adam looked at his mother.','“All of this?','She told him:','“These are things the home needs.','Adam pointed at the list.','“Are we a home or a restaurant?','His mother did not laugh.','She folded the paper,','and put it in her bag.','Then she looked at him.','“Come on,','get up and change your clothes.','Adam drank the last sip of tea.','He knew a trip to the market with his mother was never a quick trip.','He also knew that the list he had just seen would not remain the same by the time they returned.','Because his mother always remembered new things while walking.'];
yomBilSouqPageTranslations[0] = yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[0].join(' ');
yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[1] = ['Adam left with his mother at around ten o’clock.','The sun was up,','and the street was beginning to get crowded.','Some people were going to work,','others were out buying what they needed,','and shared taxis stood along the street while their drivers called out destinations.','Adam planned to take a shared taxi straight to the market.','But his mother said it was not far,','and that they could walk for a little while.','Adam looked at her.','“A little while” was a dangerous phrase when his mother used it.','Sometimes it meant five minutes.','Other times it meant half an hour.','They walked.','On the way,','they passed a bakery.','His mother stopped.','Adam looked at her.','“Aren’t we going to the market?','She said:','“Yes,','but the bread here is better.','She bought bread.','Adam took the bag.','They continued.','Two minutes later,','they passed a small shop.','His mother saw a box of tea on display at a lower price.','She stopped.','This time Adam said nothing.','She bought two boxes.','Adam carried them.','Then they passed a cleaning-supplies shop.','His mother remembered that she needed laundry detergent.','She went inside.','Adam waited at the door,','looking at the bags he was already holding before they had even reached the market.','When she came out,','she had another bag.','Adam took it from her hand.','He said:','“If we keep going like this,','we’ll go home before we ever reach the market.','His mother laughed.','“All right,','we’re almost there now.','They walked for another five minutes.','Then they began hearing the market before they could see it.','The vendors’ voices.','The sound of cars.','People bargaining.','People calling to one another.','And the sound of vegetable carts moving through the crowd.','When they entered the first street,','Adam looked ahead.','The market was packed from one end to the other.','His mother opened her bag,','and took out the list.','She said:','“We’ll start with the vegetables.','Adam took a breath.','Now the shopping trip had begun in earnest.'];
yomBilSouqPageTranslations[1] = yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[1].join(' ');
yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[2] = ['Adam’s mother had a particular vegetable seller she liked to buy from.','His name was Abu al-Abd.','His stall was at the far end of the vegetable row,','so they had to pass about ten other stalls to reach him.','Adam did not understand why.','Every stall sold tomatoes, cucumbers, and potatoes.','But his mother insisted.','She said:','“Abu al-Abd gives us good produce.','When they arrived,','Abu al-Abd spotted Adam’s mother from a distance.','He smiled,','and greeted her.','He was a man in his fifties,','standing behind a long table piled with vegetables of different colors.','Red tomatoes.','Green cucumbers.','Peppers.','Eggplants.','Lemons.','And a pile of potatoes on the side.','Adam’s mother started with the tomatoes.','She picked up the first one.','She turned it over in her hand.','She put it back.','She picked up a second one.','Adam stood beside her,','watching.','He said:','“Mom,','they’re all tomatoes.','His mother looked at him as though he had said the stupidest thing imaginable.','“They’re not all the same.','Adam fell silent.','Abu al-Abd laughed.','He told Adam:','“Stick to what you know, son.','Your mother knows what she’s doing.','Adam laughed.','His mother chose the tomatoes and cucumbers.','Then she asked the price of the potatoes.','Abu al-Abd named the price.','Adam’s mother raised her eyebrows.','She said:','“Why?','Is there gold inside them?','Abu al-Abd laughed,','and said prices had gone up for everyone.','They began negotiating the price.','Adam stood between them,','feeling as though the matter had become an official negotiation.','His mother named a price.','Abu al-Abd refused.','She raised it a little.','He said he would lose money at that price.','In the end,','they agreed on a lower price than the first one.','Abu al-Abd weighed the potatoes.','Adam’s mother smiled.','Adam looked at her.','He knew she was not pleased because the amount saved was large.','She was pleased because she had not paid the first price he quoted.','When they had finished,','Abu al-Abd packed everything into three large bags.','He held them out to Adam.','Adam took them.','His expression changed under their weight.','His mother had already started walking ahead.','He called out to her:','“Mom!','She turned around.','“What?','He lifted the bags.','“Did we come here to shop or to work out?','Abu al-Abd laughed loudly.','His mother kept walking.'];
yomBilSouqPageTranslations[2] = yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[2].join(' ');
yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[3] = ['After the vegetables,','they were supposed to go to the rice and sugar shop.','But as they walked,','they passed a clothing stall.','Hangers were packed one above another,','and shirts and trousers were stacked on a long table.','Adam’s mother slowed down.','Adam noticed.','He tried to keep walking as though he had seen nothing.','But his mother stopped.','“Adam.','He turned toward her.','She was holding a dark blue shirt.','“Come and look.','Adam raised the bags in his hands.','“Mom,','it isn’t on the list.','She told him:','“Just for a moment.','Adam knew that “just for a moment” would open a whole new door.','He came closer.','His mother held the shirt in front of him,','and looked at him.','She said the color suited him.','Adam asked the price.','The seller named a figure.','Adam put the shirt back.','His mother looked at him.','“Why?','He said:','“I have shirts.','His mother replied:','“All your shirts are the same color.','Adam was not sure whether that was really a problem.','The seller joined the conversation.','He said the shirt was good quality,','and that he could offer Adam a better price.','Adam looked at his mother.','His mother said nothing.','But her smile was unmistakable.','Adam began bargaining with the seller.','The first price.','A second price.','Then one a little lower.','In the end,','they reached an agreement.','When Adam paid,','his mother smiled.','She said:','“See?','You learned from me.','Adam took the bag containing the shirt and added it to the other bags.','He said:','“I wasn’t planning to buy anything in the first place.','His mother continued walking.','“But you bought something good.','Adam looked at the list in his mother’s hand.','The shirt was not written on it.','The bread was not written on it.','The tea was not written on it.','And they had bought the cleaning supplies before they even arrived.','By now he was certain that the list was merely a suggestion.','Not a plan.'];
yomBilSouqPageTranslations[3] = yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[3].join(' ');
yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[4] = ['They reached the large grocery store about an hour after entering the market.','Adam was tired.','His hands hurt from carrying the bags,','and he felt as though they had spent half the day there,','even though it was still only eleven thirty.','His mother took a small shopping cart inside the store.','Adam placed the bags of vegetables in it,','and felt as though he had been set free.','They started with the rice.','Then the sugar.','Then the oil.','His mother began comparing several brands.','She picked up a container.','She read the price.','She put it back.','She picked up another one.','Adam stood beside the cart,','waiting.','Half an hour later,','they reached the checkout.','The cashier began totaling their purchases.','Adam reached for his wallet to pay part of the bill.','As soon as he opened his pocket,','he could not find it.','He checked his other pocket.','Empty.','He froze.','He searched his jacket pocket.','Nothing.','His mother was busy with the cashier,','and did not notice him.','Adam put down the bags,','and began searching.','His wallet was not with him.','He felt his heart begin to race.','There was money inside it.','And his ID.','And several important papers.','He turned toward his mother.','“Mom.','She looked at him.','“What?','He said quietly:','“I don’t have my wallet.','His mother’s expression changed.','“What do you mean you don’t have it?','Adam searched his pockets a second time,','even though he knew it was not there.','He tried to remember the last time he had held it.','The shirt.','He had paid the seller.','He had put the change in his wallet.','Then… he walked away.','He looked at his mother.','“Maybe it’s at the clothing stall.','His mother asked the cashier to wait,','and left their purchases beside the checkout.','Adam hurried out of the store.','The market that had been nothing but crowds and noise minutes earlier,','now seemed much larger.','He had to retrace every step he had taken during the past hour.','And his wallet could be lying anywhere they had stopped.'];
yomBilSouqPageTranslations[4] = yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[4].join(' ');
yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[5] = ['Adam hurried toward the clothing stall.','He tried to remember every detail.','When he paid for the shirt,','he had been holding the bags in his left hand.','He took out the wallet with his right hand.','He took the change.','Then the seller placed the shirt in a bag.','Adam took it.','But where had he put the wallet?','He could not remember.','He reached the stall.','The seller was busy with another customer.','Adam could barely wait for him to finish.','He asked him:','“Excuse me,','did you find a black wallet here?','The seller thought.','He looked beneath the table.','Then beside the cardboard box.','He shook his head.','“No, son.','Adam felt his anxiety increasing.','He asked whether someone else might have taken it.','The seller said he had not seen anything.','Adam thanked him,','and started walking again.','Then he remembered Abu al-Abd’s stall.','Perhaps he had taken out the wallet there to pay for some of the groceries.','He went there.','Abu al-Abd saw him approaching quickly.','He asked him:','“What’s wrong?','Did you forget something?','Adam told him about the wallet.','Abu al-Abd called his son,','and asked whether he had found a wallet.','His son said no.','They searched beside and beneath the table.','Nothing.','Adam looked at the ground.','The market was crowded.','Hundreds of feet had passed through there since he bought the vegetables.','If the wallet had fallen on the ground,','it was unlikely to have remained there.','Abu al-Abd told him:','“Search calmly.','Maybe you put it inside a bag.','Adam remembered the bags.','He called his mother.','He asked her to search the vegetable bags and the shirt bag.','A minute later,','she told him:','“It isn’t here.','Adam ended the call.','He stood in the middle of the market,','feeling as though his mind had gone blank.','Then the bakery occurred to him.','But the bakery had been before the market,','and he was certain the wallet had still been with him afterward.','The tea shop?','That had been earlier too.','The cleaning-supplies shop?','Earlier.','He remained standing for a few seconds,','trying to reconstruct the journey in his mind.','Suddenly,','his phone rang.','It was an unfamiliar number.'];
yomBilSouqPageTranslations[5] = yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[5].join(' ');
yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[6] = ['Adam looked at the number.','On any other day,','he might not have answered.','But now he answered quickly.','“Hello?','A man’s voice came through:','“Are you Adam?','Adam was silent for a second.','“Yes.','The man asked whether he had lost a black wallet.','Adam felt as though he could breathe again.','“Yes!','Where did you find it?','The man told him he had found it on the ground near a fruit stall,','and opened it to find out who owned it.','He found an ID bearing Adam’s name,','and a small piece of paper with his phone number.','Adam had completely forgotten that the paper with his number was inside the wallet.','He asked the man where he was.','The caller turned out to own a household-goods shop at the edge of the market.','Adam hurried toward him.','Five minutes later,','he arrived.','A man in his forties stood outside the shop,','holding the wallet.','As soon as he saw Adam,','he asked for his full name to make sure the wallet belonged to him.','Adam answered.','The man held out the wallet.','Adam took it,','and opened it.','The money was inside.','His ID was inside.','Everything was in its place.','He looked at the man.','“Honestly, I don’t know how to thank you.','The man simply said:','“Don’t mention it.','Take better care of it from now on.','Adam tried to give him some money.','The man immediately refused.','Adam insisted.','The man insisted even more.','In the end,','all Adam could do was thank him again.','Before leaving,','he asked exactly where the man had found the wallet.','The man pointed toward a nearby street.','He said:','“It was beside the apple stall.','Adam told him:','“But I didn’t even buy any apples.','The man laughed.','“Maybe you didn’t buy any.','But it looks like your mother stopped there.','Adam remembered.','On their way from the vegetables to the clothing stall,','his mother had indeed stopped to ask the price of the apples.','Adam had put the bags on the ground.','And he had taken out his wallet to see how much money he had left.','That was where it had fallen.','Adam put the wallet in the inside pocket of his jacket.','He closed the zipper over it.','This time,','he was prepared to check it every five minutes.'];
yomBilSouqPageTranslations[6] = yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[6].join(' ');
yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[7] = ['When Adam returned to the large store,','he found his mother still standing beside their purchases.','As soon as she saw the wallet in his hand,','she breathed a sigh of relief.','But immediately afterward, she began:','“Don’t I always tell you to look after your things?','Adam was so happy that her words did not bother him.','He said:','“It’s all right, Mom,','I found it.','His mother asked who had found it,','and how the person knew his number.','Adam told her the story.','When she heard that the man had refused to accept money,','she prayed for him.','Then they paid the bill.','They left the store.','Adam thought the trip was over.','It was nearly one o’clock.','He was beginning to feel hungry.','And his hands could not carry anything more.','He said:','“Come on, let’s go home.','His mother opened the list.','She looked at it.','Then she said:','“We still need the fruit.','Adam stopped.','“Mom!','She said:','“What?','We came to the market to buy what we need.','Adam looked at the bags around him.','There were vegetables.','Rice.','Sugar.','Oil.','Cleaning supplies.','Bread.','Tea.','A shirt.','And several other things whose contents he had forgotten.','He said:','“We still haven’t bought what we need?','His mother laughed.','They went to the fruit stalls.','This time,','Adam stayed close to his wallet as though guarding it.','His mother bought apples.','Oranges.','And bananas.','When she picked up a bag of grapes,','Adam looked at her.','“Mom,','that’s enough.','She said:','“These are for your grandmother.','Adam fell silent.','He could never object to anything meant for his grandmother.','They bought the grapes.','And now they were truly finished.','At least,','that was what Adam thought.'];
yomBilSouqPageTranslations[7] = yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[7].join(' ');

yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[8] = ['Adam and his mother stood at the edge of the market.','The purchases around them were more than two people could comfortably carry.','His mother looked at the bags.','Then at Adam.','Adam said:','“Don’t look at me.','His mother laughed.','She said they should take a taxi.','Adam agreed before she had finished the sentence.','This time he was not prepared to walk,','or transfer the shopping from one shared taxi to another.','They stopped a taxi.','The driver got out,','and helped them put the bags in the trunk.','But the trunk could not hold everything.','They placed several bags on the back seat.','Adam’s mother sat beside them.','Adam sat in front.','The car moved off.','For the first time that morning,','Adam sat without holding anything.','He rested his head against the seat.','He watched the market recede through the window.','From inside the car,','the market seemed calmer.','But he could still hear the vendors calling in the distance.','His mother checked the list one final time.','Suddenly she said:','“We forgot…” Adam quickly turned toward her.','“No.','His mother laughed.','“I was going to say we forgot to get something for Nour.','Adam looked out the window.','“Nour is sitting comfortably at home.','She gets nothing.','His mother said Nour might be upset.','Adam replied:','“Let her be upset.','The driver laughed.','His mother laughed too.','A little later,','Adam said:','“By the way,','the shirt is mine.','It isn’t a gift for Nour.','His mother said:','“I didn’t mean the shirt.','Adam fell silent.','Then he remembered the sweet shop at the edge of their neighborhood.','He said:','“We’ll get her something near home.','His mother agreed.','Before they reached home,','they stopped at a small shop,','and Adam bought Nour some chocolate.','When he returned to the taxi,','his mother said:','“See?','It’s better than going home empty-handed for her.','Adam looked at the car packed with bags.','He wanted to ask:','Which hand is empty?','But he remained silent.','He was tired of arguing.'];
yomBilSouqPageTranslations[8] = yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[8].join(' ');
yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[9] = ['When they reached the entrance to the building,','Adam got out of the taxi and opened the trunk.','He looked at the bags.','Then he looked up the stairs.','The apartment was on the second floor.','This time it felt as though it were on the twentieth.','The driver helped him unload the shopping at the building entrance.','Adam thanked him,','and paid the fare.','Then the second journey began.','From the building entrance to the apartment door.','He took four bags on the first trip.','He went up.','He came down.','He took three more.','He went up.','He came down.','On the third trip,','he found Yusuf coming down the stairs.','Yusuf stopped,','and looked at the bags.','“What is all this?','Adam said:','“My mother went out to get a few things.','Yusuf laughed.','He took two bags from Adam,','and helped him carry them upstairs.','When they entered the apartment,','Nour was sitting in the living room holding her phone.','She looked at the bags.','“You bought all of this?','Adam put the final bag on the floor.','He did not answer.','He took the chocolate from his pocket,','and tossed it to her.','Nour caught it.','She smiled.','“Is this for me?','Adam said:','“No,','it’s for the neighbor.','Yes, it’s for you.','His mother began arranging the groceries in the kitchen.','Adam put the shirt in his room.','Then he took the wallet from his inside pocket.','He opened it.','Everything was in its place.','He kept looking at it for a moment.','Of everything that had happened during the trip,','that moment had frightened him the most.','What if the man had not found it?','Or if someone else had seen it first?','Things could have turned out much worse.','He put the wallet in the drawer.','Then he returned to the living room.','His mother was still putting things away.','Nour was eating the chocolate.','And his father had returned from an errand,','and stood staring at the quantity of shopping.','He asked:','“Did you buy the entire market?','Adam laughed.','He said:','“Finally, someone understands me.','His mother looked at them,','and said these supplies would last for a while,','so they would not need to visit the market again soon.','Adam sat on the sofa.','“How soon is soon?','She said:','“Maybe next week.','Adam raised his head.','“That is soon!','His father laughed.','Nour laughed.','Even his mother smiled.','Adam rested his head against the sofa.','Since morning, he had thought the market would be a boring errand.','But now,','when he thought back over the day,','he found an entire story in it.','Bargaining over potatoes.','A shirt that was not on the list.','A lost wallet.','A stranger who returned it.','More bags than he had hands.','And his mother,','from the beginning of the trip to the end,','convinced that they had bought only “a few things.”','He looked at the new shirt, whose bag sat beside his bedroom door.','He smiled.','After all that effort,','there was one thing he did not want to admit.','His mother had been right.','He really did like the shirt.'];
yomBilSouqPageTranslations[9] = yomBilSouqClauseTranslations[9].join(' ');

const rihlaAlBahrPageTranslations = Array(10).fill('');
const rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations = Array(10).fill(null);
rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[0] = ['For more than a week, Adam, Samer, and Yusuf had been talking about going to the sea.','Every time they agreed on a day,','something came up and ruined the plan.','Once Adam had to work overtime.','Another time Samer had an errand with his family.','And once Yusuf had to remain at the shop until late.','In the end,','they agreed on Friday.','They did not have an elaborate plan.','They wanted to leave in the afternoon,','sit by the sea,','bring some light food,','and return home after sunset.','Adam liked the idea as soon as they discussed it.','It had been a while since he had gone to the sea with his friends.','Sometimes he passed nearby,','or saw it from a distance,','but sitting on the sand was different.','On Thursday night,','Samer messaged the group:','“Nobody start making excuses tomorrow.','Everyone must be ready at three.','Yusuf replied:','“I’m ready.','Adam wrote:','“Me too.','Then Samer sent another message:','“Especially you, Adam.','Don’t say: I’ll be there in a little while.','Adam understood what he meant.','Ever since the last-bus incident,','Samer used the phrase “a little while” against him at every opportunity.','Adam sent a laughing emoji,','and put down his phone.','The next day,','he woke at his leisure.','It was Friday,','and he did not have work.','He ate breakfast with his family,','then went to his room.','At around one o’clock,','he opened the wardrobe and began deciding what to wear.','The weather was warm,','so he chose lightweight trousers and a short-sleeved shirt.','He put a small towel in his bag,','a bottle of water,','and his phone charger.','When his mother saw him getting ready,','she asked where he was going.','He told her he was going to the sea with Samer and Yusuf.','His mother nodded.','Then she asked:','“Are you going swimming?','Adam said he did not know.','His mother looked at him.','“If the sea is rough,','don’t go in.','Adam smiled.','He was twenty-four years old,','but his mother still gave him the same warning she had given him as a child.','He said:','“All right, Mom.','Then she put a container holding several sandwiches in his bag.','Adam objected.','He said they would buy food there.','His mother closed the bag.','“Keep them with you.','They’ll come in handy.','Adam did not argue.','He had learned long ago that food his mother put in his bag always ended up being useful.','At two thirty,','he was ready.','This time,','he had no intention of being late.'];
rihlaAlBahrPageTranslations[0] = rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[0].join(' ');
rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[1] = ['They agreed to meet at the shared-taxi stop.','Adam arrived first.','He checked the time.','It was ten to three.','He smiled to himself.','He messaged the group:','“I’m here.','Samer replied:','“Impossible.','Yusuf sent:','“Take a picture of the clock.','Adam laughed.','Five minutes later,','Yusuf arrived.','He was carrying a large bag filled with water and juice.','Adam asked:','“What did you bring?','Yusuf opened the bag.','It contained bottles of water,','juice,','and a bag of sunflower seeds.','Adam said:','“We’re going to sit there for two hours,','not set up camp.','Yusuf replied:','“Keep them.','They’ll come in handy.','Adam laughed.','It was the same phrase his mother had used.','At five past three,','Samer still had not arrived.','Adam messaged him:','“Where are you?','The reply came:','“I’ll be there in a little while.','Adam looked at Yusuf.','Yusuf read the message on Adam’s phone,','and began laughing.','Adam said:','“Now I understand why that phrase is so annoying.','Samer arrived fifteen minutes later.','As soon as Adam saw him,','he said:','“Weren’t you the one who said three o’clock?','Samer said he was late because his mother had asked him to pick something up from the shop.','Adam did not entirely believe him.','But he did not want to waste any more time.','They boarded the shared taxi.','There were many people inside,','but they found three seats in a row at the back.','The shared taxi moved off.','With every street that brought them closer to the sea,','the atmosphere changed.','The wind grew stronger.','And they began to smell the water.','Samer opened the window.','Adam told him to close it a little,','because the wind was hitting them in the face.','Samer refused.','He said:','“This is the best part of the journey.','Adam looked out the window.','In the distance,','he began to see the color of the sea.','Deep blue,','with a wide sky above it.','He felt the week’s exhaustion begin to ease before they had even left the shared taxi.'];
rihlaAlBahrPageTranslations[1] = rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[1].join(' ');
rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[2] = ['They got out near the sea.','As soon as they opened the shared taxi’s door,','the wind struck their faces.','It was stronger than the air in their neighborhood,','and carried a distinct smell of salt.','They walked toward the beach.','The closer they came,','the louder the waves became.','There were many people.','Families sitting on the sand.','Children playing football.','Young men standing by the water.','And vendors selling coffee, corn, and lupini beans all along the beach.','Samer took off his shoes as soon as he reached the sand.','He carried them in his hand,','and continued barefoot.','Yusuf did the same.','Adam kept his shoes on.','Samer looked at him.','“Did you come to the sea or to work?','Adam said the sand would fill his shoes.','Samer replied:','“That’s why you take them off.','In the end,','Adam took his off too.','As soon as he walked on the sand,','he felt its warmth beneath his feet.','They approached the water.','The waves were moderate.','Not very calm,','and not high.','Samer stepped straight into the water.','When the first wave reached him,','he jumped backward.','The water was cold.','Yusuf laughed at him.','Then Yusuf stepped in too,','and did exactly the same thing.','Adam remained standing on the wet sand.','A wave reached his feet.','The water truly was cold,','but the feeling was pleasant.','They stayed beside the water for several minutes.','Then they looked for somewhere to sit.','They found a slightly quieter spot,','near an old beach umbrella.','Adam spread his small towel on the sand.','Samer looked at it.','“Are you the only one who’s going to sit on that?','Adam said:','“You didn’t bring anything to spread out.','Yusuf spread out a large plastic bag.','Samer sat directly on the sand.','He said:','“I came to the sea.','I’m not afraid of the sand.','Adam sat down.','He looked ahead.','The sea stretched until it disappeared into the horizon.','From where he sat,','he could see nothing but water and sky.','For several minutes,','none of them said anything.','The sound of the waves was enough.'];
rihlaAlBahrPageTranslations[2] = rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[2].join(' ');
rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[3] = ['After they had been sitting for a while,','Yusuf opened the bag of sunflower seeds.','Samer took some before Yusuf could offer him any.','Yusuf looked at him.','“I’m the one who brought those.','Samer replied:','“We’re friends.','There’s no such thing as yours and mine.','Yusuf said:','“Good.','Hand over your wallet.','Samer laughed.','Adam sat between them, looking at the sea.','A little later,','the conversation began moving from one subject to another.','Samer mentioned one of their old friends who had become engaged.','Yusuf asked Adam whether his family still brought up marriage at every family gathering.','Adam sighed.','He said the subject had become part of the meal.','Just like the rice and salad.','Samer laughed.','He told him:','“All right,','next Friday we’ll come and find you a bride from the sea.','Adam threw some sand at him.','They laughed.','Then the conversation became quieter.','Yusuf talked about his job at the shop,','and said he had begun thinking about looking for a better one.','The salary was not enough,','and the commute was long.','Samer said he also felt stuck in the same place,','and did not know what he wanted to do in a year or two.','Adam listened to them.','He remembered himself before he found work.','He had thought that as soon as he found a job,','all the questions would disappear.','But after he began working,','he discovered that every stage brought new questions.','Should he remain in this job?','Would the salary be enough?','Was there a better opportunity?','Where did he see himself in a few years?','He looked at the sea.','He said quietly:','“Maybe nobody has everything figured out.','Samer nodded.','Yusuf said it was enough for a person to know the next step.','They fell silent.','The waves rose and fell before them.','Adam thought Yusuf was right.','A person did not need to see the entire road.','Maybe it was enough to know where to place the next footstep.','Then Samer broke the silence.','He said:','“Good.','After all that wisdom,','who’s going to get the coffee?','Adam and Yusuf looked at him.','Samer smiled.','“Adam.','Adam asked:','“Why me?','Samer replied:','“Because you’re the closest one standing.','Adam looked at himself.','He was sitting down, just like them.','But in the end, he stood up.'];
rihlaAlBahrPageTranslations[3] = rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[3].join(' ');
rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[4] = ['Adam went to buy three cups of coffee from a man with a nearby cart.','When he returned,','Samer and Yusuf were standing.','Several young men in front of them were playing football on the sand.','Samer said:','“They need one more player.','Adam looked at the coffee in his hand.','“What about the coffee?','Yusuf took his cup.','Samer took the second one.','That left Adam’s cup.','He placed it beside the bag.','They joined the game.','Playing on the sand was harder than playing on a field.','Whenever Adam ran,','his feet sank slightly.','After five minutes,','he was breathing heavily.','Samer was the most enthusiastic of them all.','He chased the ball as though the match were a cup final.','Yusuf laughed at him.','During one play,','Samer kicked the ball hard.','Instead of going toward the goal,','it flew toward the water.','Everyone stopped.','The ball landed on the wet sand,','and a small wave carried it away.','Samer ran after it.','He reached the water,','and tried to grab it.','The waves pulled it slightly farther out.','Samer went in deeper.','The water reached his knees.','Adam stood on the sand,','laughing.','He said:','“Leave it!','Samer refused.','“The ball isn’t ours!','He took another two steps.','At that moment,','a stronger wave arrived.','It struck Samer from the side.','Samer lost his balance.','In an instant,','he fell into the water.','Adam and Yusuf began laughing.','Samer stood up.','From head to toe,','he was soaked.','His shirt.','His trousers.','His hair.','Everything.','And he was holding the ball in his hand.','He raised it above his head.','“I got it!','Adam could not stop laughing.','Yusuf sat down on the sand from laughing so hard.','Samer came out of the water.','He approached them.','Adam saw the look on his face,','and knew there was trouble.','He backed away.','Samer ran after him,','and began splashing him with water from his soaked shirt.','Within a minute,','all three were laughing and running across the sand like little children.'];
rihlaAlBahrPageTranslations[4] = rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[4].join(' ');
rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[5] = ['After they finished playing,','they returned to their spot.','Samer was soaked,','and sand clung to his legs and trousers.','Adam told him to sit in the sun so he could dry off a little.','Samer said it was not a problem,','and that the weather was warm.','They sat down.','Adam reached for his bag to take out the sandwiches.','It was not where he had left it.','He looked around.','The towel was there.','Yusuf’s bag was there.','Their shoes were there.','But Adam’s bag was gone.','He stood up.','He said:','“Where’s my bag?','Samer was wringing out the edge of his shirt.','At first, he did not seem concerned.','“It was here.','Adam said:','“It isn’t here.','Yusuf stood up too.','They began looking around.','There were many people on the beach.','Some had passed beside them while they were playing.','Adam felt anxiety tightening in his chest.','His phone was inside the bag.','His charger.','Money.','And the house keys.','He said:','“My phone is in it.','This time,','Samer stood up immediately.','They split up.','Adam went toward the water.','Samer circled the area where they had been playing.','Yusuf went to ask the coffee vendor.','Adam searched with his eyes fixed on the sand.','Every black bag he saw from a distance,','he thought was his.','But whenever he came closer,','it belonged to someone else.','He returned to their spot.','Samer arrived at the same moment.','He shook his head.','He had not found it.','Two minutes later,','Yusuf came back.','He said the coffee vendor had not seen anything.','Adam put his hands on his head.','A few weeks earlier,','he had lost his wallet at the market.','Now he had lost his entire bag at the sea.','Samer said:','“Maybe someone picked it up by mistake.','Adam looked at him.','“A whole bag by mistake?','Samer fell silent.','It was not a good answer.','They began searching again.','This time,','Adam asked the people sitting near their spot.','A family sitting on the sand.','Two young men beside an umbrella.','A man selling lupini beans.','Nobody had seen it.','After ten minutes,','Adam began to believe that someone had taken it.','And that was the worst possibility.'];
rihlaAlBahrPageTranslations[5] = rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[5].join(' ');
rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[6] = ['Yusuf took out his phone.','He said:','“Call your phone.','Adam told him his phone was on silent.','Samer said:','“Try anyway.','Yusuf called.','They all stood silently.','Of course,','they heard nothing.','Then Yusuf said:','“Wait… someone answered.','Adam quickly moved closer.','Yusuf turned on the speaker.','A young boy’s voice came through:','“Hello?','Adam and Samer looked at each other.','Yusuf asked:','“Whose phone do you have?','The boy said he had found a bag on the sand,','and the phone was inside it.','Adam felt as though a weight had been lifted from his chest.','He quickly asked:','“Where are you?','The boy said he was sitting with his family near a corn cart.','Adam looked around.','There was more than one cart.','Yusuf asked the boy what color the nearby umbrella was.','He said it was blue and white.','Samer pointed into the distance.','A blue-and-white umbrella stood near a cart.','They hurried toward it.','When they arrived,','they found a family sitting on the sand.','A boy of about ten was holding Adam’s phone.','Beside his father,','sat Adam’s bag.','Adam took a deep breath.','He greeted the family,','and thanked them.','The boy’s father said his son had found the bag near the water.','He was afraid the waves would reach it,','so he picked it up and brought it to the family.','Adam looked at the boy.','He said:','“Thank you so much.','The boy smiled shyly.','Adam opened the bag.','His phone.','The money.','The keys.','Everything was there.','He asked the boy’s father exactly where they had found it.','The man pointed toward the place where they had sat before the football game.','Adam understood what had happened.','When they got up to play,','the waves had gradually moved closer.','Perhaps one wave had reached near the bag,','and the boy saw it and assumed it had been abandoned.','Adam thanked them again.','After they walked away,','Samer said:','“You have a problem with your belongings.','Adam looked at him.','“Me?','You’re the one who made us play.','Samer replied:','“I didn’t tell you to leave the bag behind.','Yusuf laughed.','Adam put the bag over his shoulder.','This time,','he decided it would not leave his shoulder until he went home.'];
rihlaAlBahrPageTranslations[6] = rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[6].join(' ');
rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[7] = ['After all that searching,','they were hungry.','They sat farther away from the water.','Adam opened the bag.','He took out the container of sandwiches his mother had packed.','Samer saw it.','“What’s that?','Adam opened the container.','It held four sandwiches.','Cheese.','Za’atar.','And two labneh-and-cucumber sandwiches.','Yusuf reached out his hand.','Adam moved the container away.','“Weren’t you the one who said there’s no such thing as yours and mine?','Yusuf laughed.','“Samer said that,','not me.','Samer reached out too.','Adam said:','“I’ve been telling my mother since this morning that we’d buy food.','Samer took a za’atar sandwich.','“Give her my regards.','They sat eating.','Samer was still half soaked,','but the sun had dried much of his clothing.','Yusuf opened the juice.','Adam looked at the sea.','The sun had begun to set.','The color of the sky changed slightly.','The blue softened,','and a pale orange began appearing near the horizon.','There were fewer people on the beach now too.','Some families gathered their belongings.','The children who had played since the afternoon were growing tired.','The three friends sat quietly.','Then Samer said:','“Even though I fell into the water,','today was good.','Yusuf replied:','“You fell in because you’re an idiot.','Samer threw a sunflower-seed shell at him.','Adam laughed.','He said:','“And I lost my bag.','Samer replied:','“So it was a normal day.','They laughed.','Then they fell silent again.','Some things that happen with friends do not seem important while they are happening.','A fall into the water.','A bag lost for ten minutes.','Sandwiches on the sand.','But months later,','those might be the very things they remember.','Not what they discussed that day.','But who was with them.','And how much they laughed.'];
rihlaAlBahrPageTranslations[7] = rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[7].join(' ');

rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[8] = ['After sunset,','the air began to cool.','Adam put on a light jacket he had packed in the bag.','Samer had brought nothing.','His clothes were almost dry,','but the breeze was making him cold.','He folded his arms across his chest.','He said:','“Come on, let’s go home.','Yusuf looked at him.','“Weren’t you the one who wanted to stay?','Samer said:','“I’d stay if I weren’t soaked.','They gathered their belongings.','Adam checked the bag.','Phone.','Keys.','Wallet.','Charger.','Everything.','Yusuf saw him.','He said:','“Check it one more time.','Adam replied:','“Knock it off.','They put on their shoes.','The problem was that their feet were covered in sand.','Samer tried to clean his feet with his hand.','But whenever he put on a shoe,','he felt the sand inside it.','In the end,','he said:','“Forget it.','I’ll clean them at home.','They walked toward the stop.','As they left the beach,','Adam turned for one final look at the sea.','The world had grown darker.','A few lights began appearing along the beach.','The waves remained the same.','Rising.','And falling.','Unconcerned with whether people arrived or left.','They reached the stop.','This time,','Adam was the one who asked the driver:','“How late do the shared taxis run?','Samer looked at him,','and began laughing.','Adam said:','“It isn’t happening again.','The driver said there was still plenty of time.','They got in.','Samer sat beside the window.','Two minutes later,','he began shivering from the wind.','Adam told him:','“Close the window.','Samer closed it without arguing.','Yusuf laughed.','On the way,','they were all tired.','They did not talk much.','Samer rested his head against the window.','Yusuf opened his phone.','Adam watched the lights pass outside.','He could feel sand inside his shoes.','His hair was filled with wind and salt.','And his face felt tight from the sun.','But he was happy.'];
rihlaAlBahrPageTranslations[8] = rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[8].join(' ');
rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[9] = ['Adam reached home at around nine o’clock.','As soon as he opened the door,','his mother was in the living room.','She looked at him.','Then she sniffed the air around him.','She said:','“Did you bring the sea into the house with you?','Adam laughed.','He really did smell of seawater and sand.','He took off his shoes at the door.','As soon as he turned them over,','sand spilled onto the floor.','His mother looked at him.','Adam said:','“I didn’t mean to.','He called for Nour to bring the broom.','From her room,','she replied:','“You made the mess,','you clean it.','Adam found nobody on his side.','He took the broom,','and swept up the sand.','Then he entered the kitchen,','and took the empty container from his bag.','His mother saw it.','“Did you eat the sandwiches?','Adam said:','“Yes.','His mother smiled a small smile of triumph.','She did not say:','“Didn’t I tell you?','But her face said it for her.','Adam went into the bathroom.','When he washed his face,','a little sand fell from his hair.','He laughed.','After changing his clothes,','he sat on the bed and opened his phone.','The group chat was full of pictures.','Yusuf had photographed Samer after he fell into the water.','His shirt clung to his body,','his hair hung over his face,','and he held the ball above his head.','Adam began laughing again.','Samer had written:','“I’ll be angry with anyone who sends this picture to somebody else.','Yusuf replied:','“Too late—it has reached half of Gaza.','Samer sent back a rude word.','Adam laughed even harder.','Then he saw another picture.','The three of them were sitting on the sand before sunset.','The picture was not carefully posed.','Samer was holding a glass of juice.','Yusuf was looking in another direction.','And Adam’s eyes were half closed against the sun.','But he liked the picture.','He saved it to his phone.','Before going to sleep,','he opened the window.','The air in the neighborhood was different from the sea breeze.','Calmer.','And slightly warmer.','He looked at the sky.','He thought about the day.','Nothing major had happened.','They went.','They sat.','They played.','Samer fell into the water.','They lost a bag and found it.','They ate.','And they went home.','But Adam knew that after some time they would remember that day,','and laugh about the same moments.','Not because the trip to the sea had been important.','But because good days do not always need a grand reason.','Sometimes,','they need three friends.','A little time.','Sandwiches from home.','And an open sea before them.','He closed the window.','And put his phone on the charger.','Before turning off the light,','a message arrived from Samer:','“Shall we do it again next Friday?','Adam smiled.','He wrote:','“Yes.','But this time, you’re bringing the food.','Samer replied:','“We’ll see.','Adam knew that meant his mother would put sandwiches in his bag again.','And honestly,','he did not mind.'];
rihlaAlBahrPageTranslations[9] = rihlaAlBahrClauseTranslations[9].join(' ');

const bilMataamPageTranslations = Array(10).fill('');
const bilMataamClauseTranslations = Array(10).fill(null);
bilMataamClauseTranslations[0] = ['A week after the trip to the sea,','Adam was sitting with Samer and Yusuf on the rooftop.','The evening was calm,','the breeze was light,','and each of them had a glass of tea.','From the start, Samer kept complaining that he was hungry.','Yusuf told him to go make himself a sandwich.','Samer replied that he was not in the mood for food from home.','Adam looked at him.','“Ever since you fell into the sea, nothing has been good enough for you.','Samer told him it had nothing to do with the sea,','and that for some time he had wanted to visit a new restaurant near his workplace.','Yusuf asked him:','“Is it expensive?','Samer shrugged.','“Not very.','Adam laughed.','He knew that “not very” could mean almost anything.','Samer opened his phone,','and showed them pictures of the restaurant.','The place looked stylish.','Wooden tables.','Soft lighting.','And carefully arranged food that made Adam hungry even though he had already eaten dinner.','Yusuf said:','“Let’s go on Thursday.','Adam thought for a moment.','Thursday after work suited him.','Samer was delighted.','He began describing the food he had seen in the pictures,','saying they served grilled meats,','burgers,','shawarma,','and large platters meant for several people.','Adam told him:','“All right,','we’ll go.','But I don’t want to hear half an hour about the menu.','Samer closed his phone.','Then opened it again.','“Look at this platter.','Adam looked at Yusuf.','Yusuf laughed.','The plan was settled.','On Thursday after work,','they would try the new restaurant.','To Adam,','it was a simple outing.','They would go.','Eat.','And return home.','But Adam should have learned from all his previous outings.','The outings that most often begin with the words:','“A simple outing,”','are the ones that produce the longest stories.'];
bilMataamPageTranslations[0] = bilMataamClauseTranslations[0].join(' ');
bilMataamClauseTranslations[1] = ['On Thursday,','Adam finished work at four thirty.','Early that morning,','Samer had messaged the group:','“Nobody eat before we meet.','Adam read the message at noon,','while sitting on his lunch break with a sandwich in front of him.','He replied:','“Too late.','I’m eating.','Samer answered:','“You ruined the plan.','Adam did not care.','He knew that if he ate nothing from noon until six,','he would be the first person to order half the menu.','After his shift ended,','he left the company and messaged Yusuf that he was on his way.','They agreed to meet near the restaurant.','Adam arrived at around five thirty.','Yusuf was standing outside a shop beside the restaurant.','Samer had not arrived yet.','Adam looked at Yusuf.','Neither of them said anything.','But they both knew the phrase.','“I’ll be there in a little while.','Five minutes later,','Samer arrived.','He was wearing a new shirt,','and had styled his hair so carefully that Adam looked him up and down.','He said:','“We’re going out to eat,','not to a wedding.','Samer replied:','“A person should look presentable.','Yusuf pointed at Adam’s shirt.','“Adam came straight from work.','Samer said:','“You can tell.','Adam looked at him.','“What do you mean?','Samer laughed and kept walking.','The restaurant was nearby.','From the outside,','it looked even better than in the pictures.','A large glass front.','And a sign bearing the restaurant’s name in large lettering.','Through the glass, they could see many people seated inside.','As they approached the door,','Samer stopped.','He looked inside.','He said:','“It looks crowded.','Adam replied:','“Weren’t you the one who insisted we come?','They entered.','As soon as they went in,','a young staff member approached and asked how many were in their party.','Samer said:','“Three.','The young man looked across the dining room.','Then he told them:','“Would you mind waiting a little?','Adam looked at Samer.','Samer smiled.','“How long is a little?','The employee replied:','“About fifteen minutes.','Adam sighed.','The words “about fifteen minutes” were the first sign that dinner would not be as quick as he had expected.'];
bilMataamPageTranslations[1] = bilMataamClauseTranslations[1].join(' ');
bilMataamClauseTranslations[2] = ['They sat on three chairs near the door.','Every few moments, someone left the restaurant,','and new people entered.','The staff moved quickly between the tables.','The clatter of dishes,','the conversations,','and the soft music all blended together.','Samer was delighted.','He kept watching the dishes coming out of the kitchen.','Whenever a server passed carrying a plate,','he raised his head.','“That looks good.','A minute later:','“Look at that.','Then:','“No,','that one is better.','Adam said:','“Are you going to order everything?','Samer replied:','“We’ll see.','Yusuf was holding his phone.','He said they should look at the menu now so they would not spend half an hour choosing after being seated.','Samer opened the restaurant’s menu on his phone.','Adam moved closer.','The menu was longer than he expected.','Appetizers.','Salads.','Soups.','Grilled meats.','Main dishes.','Sandwiches.','Desserts.','And drinks.','Samer began reading the names.','Adam stopped him.','“Choose one thing and be done with it.','Samer looked at him as though Adam had insulted him.','“We came to try the restaurant.','Not to eat and run away.','Yusuf laughed.','After fifteen minutes,','nobody had called them.','Adam checked the time.','After twenty minutes,','Samer got up and went to ask the employee.','He returned.','He said:','“Five minutes.','Adam shook his head.','Ten minutes later,','the employee called them.','They followed him.','They passed between the tables until they reached a small table in the corner.','It had four chairs.','They sat down.','The employee placed three menus in front of them.','He said:','“Here you are.','Samer took the menu,','and opened the first page.','Adam looked at him.','Samer had memorized half the menu from his phone.','Yet he still opened it as though seeing it for the first time.'];
bilMataamPageTranslations[2] = bilMataamClauseTranslations[2].join(' ');

bilMataamClauseTranslations[3] = ['Adam read the menu calmly.','Many things appealed to him,','but the prices made him start reading again from the beginning.','He looked at Samer.','“Is this what you call not very expensive?','Samer shrugged.','“It’s normal.','Yusuf was calculating mentally.','He said:','“If each of us orders a separate meal,','it will be expensive.','Samer suggested a large mixed-grill platter for the three of them,','with appetizers.','Adam agreed.','It was easier than having everyone keep searching.','But Samer was not finished.','He said:','“And let’s get fries.','Yusuf said the platter already came with fries.','Samer replied:','“But only a few.','Adam said:','“You haven’t seen the platter before.','Samer said:','“You can tell from the picture.','Then he suggested hummus.','And mutabbal.','And salad.','Adam said:','“You’ve ordered food for six people.','Samer replied:','“We’re hungry.','Yusuf looked at Adam.','“He’s hungry.','In the end,','they agreed on a large mixed-grill platter,','hummus,','salad,','and extra fries.','The employee came over.','Samer began ordering.','When he reached the drinks,','he asked:','“What do you want?','Adam said:','“Water.','Yusuf said:','“Water.','Samer looked at them.','“What do you mean, water?','Let’s get juice.','Adam said:','“You get juice.','Samer ordered juice for himself.','The employee wrote everything down.','Then asked:','“Anything else?','Adam and Yusuf answered at the same time:','“No.','Samer was about to speak.','Adam looked at him.','Samer fell silent.','The employee took the menus and left.','Adam leaned back in his chair.','Now they only had to wait for the food.','But five minutes later,','Samer said:','“We should have ordered soup.','Adam did not reply.','Yusuf said:','“If you call the employee back,','I’m going home.','Samer fell silent.'];
bilMataamPageTranslations[3] = bilMataamClauseTranslations[3].join(' ');

bilMataamClauseTranslations[4] = ['After about twenty minutes,','the food began arriving.','First came the hummus, salad, and fries.','Samer began eating fries before the main platter arrived.','Adam said:','“Wait.','Samer replied:','“I haven’t eaten since noon.','Adam reminded him that he was the one who had told them not to eat.','Samer said:','“So we would arrive hungry.','Yusuf said:','“You succeeded.','Then the employee arrived with a large platter.','He placed it before them.','Adam looked at it.','It contained fried chicken,','small burgers,','and sauces.','Samer stopped eating.','Yusuf looked at the platter.','Then at Samer.','He said:','“This isn’t what we ordered.','Samer nodded.','He called the employee.','The employee came over.','Samer told him they had ordered the mixed-grill platter.','The employee looked at the slip in his hand.','Then at the platter.','His expression changed slightly.','He apologized.','He said the platter belonged to another table.','He picked it up,','and left.','Samer kept watching it go.','He said:','“It looked delicious.','Adam laughed.','“Another minute and you would have eaten from it.','Samer did not deny it.','A few minutes later,','the employee returned.','He said their platter would be delayed a little,','because the kitchen was busy.','Samer asked:','“How long is a little?','The employee said:','“About ten minutes.','Adam and Yusuf looked at each other.','The same word.','About.','They sat waiting.','Samer finished half the fries.','Adam began grabbing his hand whenever he reached toward the plate.','Ten minutes later,','nothing had arrived.','After fifteen minutes,','Samer was about to get up and ask.','But before he stood,','he saw the employee approaching from afar with a large platter.','This time it looked right.','Meat.','Chicken.','Kebab.','Bread.','And fries.','He placed it before them.','Samer looked at Adam.','He said:','“See?','The fries that come with it are too few.','Adam looked at the pile of fries.','Then at Samer.','There was no point arguing.'];
bilMataamPageTranslations[4] = bilMataamClauseTranslations[4].join(' ');
bilMataamClauseTranslations[5] = ['For the first few minutes,','nobody spoke.','All three were hungry,','and the food was delicious.','Adam took a piece of chicken.','Yusuf started with the kebab.','Samer tried a little of everything.','After a while,','they began slowing down.','The platter was larger than they had expected.','And of the extra fries Samer had insisted on,','half remained.','Adam said:','“Didn’t I tell you?','Samer was holding a piece of bread.','He replied:','“We’re still taking our time.','Ten minutes later,','even Samer began eating more slowly.','Yusuf leaned back in his chair.','He said:','“I’m done.','Adam said:','“Me too.','Samer looked at the platter.','There was still food on it.','He said:','“It would be a shame to waste it.','Adam replied:','“Take it with you.','Samer said he did not feel like carrying food on the way home.','Yusuf laughed.','“But you felt like ordering it.','Samer fell silent.','A little later,','they asked the employee to pack the remaining food in a container.','Samer looked at Yusuf.','He said:','“You take it.','Yusuf refused.','Adam said:','“You ordered it.','You’re taking it.','Samer sighed.','He accepted.','After they finished,','Samer opened the dessert menu.','Adam looked at him.','“Impossible.','Samer said:','“Let’s just look.','Yusuf pulled the menu from his hand and closed it.','“No dessert.','Samer replied:','“We came to try the restaurant.','Adam said:','“We tried it.','That’s enough.','Samer tried to persuade them to order knafeh.','Then cake.','Then he suggested ordering one plate to share.','Yusuf raised his hand to the employee.','Samer smiled.','He thought Yusuf had agreed.','But when the employee arrived,','Yusuf said:','“The bill,','please.','Samer looked at him.','Adam began laughing.'];
bilMataamPageTranslations[5] = bilMataamClauseTranslations[5].join(' ');

bilMataamClauseTranslations[6] = ['A few minutes later,','the employee came and placed the bill on the table.','Samer picked it up first.','He looked at the total.','He stopped laughing.','Adam noticed his expression.','He held out his hand.','“Give it to me.','He took the bill.','He looked at the amount.','Then at Samer.','He said:','“Not very expensive?','Yusuf took the bill.','He began reviewing the items.','The mixed-grill platter.','The hummus.','The salad.','The fries.','The juice.','The water.','Everything was correct.','But one dish they had not ordered appeared on the bill.','Yusuf pointed to it.','“What’s this?','Samer read the name.','It was the chicken platter mistakenly brought at the beginning.','Adam looked at Samer.','“See?','They charged us for it just because you wished you could eat it.','Samer laughed.','He called the employee.','He explained the problem.','The employee took the bill and left.','A little later,','he returned with a new bill.','He apologized,','and said the platter had accidentally been added to their table when it first arrived.','The total went down.','Samer said:','“Now it’s reasonable.','Yusuf looked at him.','“Five minutes ago your face had turned yellow.','Samer said he had only been surprised.','Adam replied:','“Yes,','obviously.','They decided to divide the bill among the three of them.','Samer said the juice was his alone,','so he would pay extra for it.','Yusuf said that was fair.','Adam began calculating on his phone.','Each person’s share was not small,','but it was less than they had initially feared.','Adam took out his wallet.','Before opening it,','he touched his pocket to make sure it was there.','Yusuf noticed.','He laughed.','“Are you still afraid of losing it?','Adam said:','“After the market and the sea,','yes.','Samer held out his hand.','“Let me hold it for you.','Adam moved it away from him.','“You’re the last person I’d trust.','They paid.','The employee brought their change.','Before they stood up,','he placed three small pieces of dessert on the table.','He said:','“Compliments of the restaurant.','Samer looked at Adam and Yusuf.','He smiled broadly.','“See?','Dessert came by itself.','Adam shook his head.','In the end,','Samer ate all three pieces.'];
bilMataamPageTranslations[6] = bilMataamClauseTranslations[6].join(' ');

bilMataamClauseTranslations[7] = ['They left the restaurant at around eight thirty.','The air outside was colder than when they had entered.','Samer held the container of leftover food.','Adam looked at it.','He said:','“Be careful not to forget it.','Samer replied:','“I’m not you.','Yusuf said:','“You once forgot your phone at university.','Samer replied:','“That was a long time ago.','They walked toward the stop.','They were so full that even walking felt heavy.','Samer said:','“We shouldn’t have ordered extra fries.','Adam and Yusuf stopped.','They looked at him.','Samer said:','“All right,','I admit it.','Adam said:','“Say it again.','Samer refused.','They continued walking.','Before reaching the stop,','they passed a small shop.','Yusuf said he wanted to buy water.','He went inside.','Adam and Samer waited outside.','Samer placed the food container on the edge of the shop window so he could take out his phone.','A minute later,','Yusuf came out.','They continued walking.','They reached the stop.','Samer said:','“Where’s the container?','All three fell silent.','Adam looked at Samer’s hand.','Empty.','Samer stared at his own hand in disbelief.','“I had it with me.','Yusuf said:','“You put it on the shop window.','Samer quickly turned around.','He ran toward the shop.','Adam and Yusuf remained where they were.','Adam said:','“It wasn’t me.','Yusuf laughed.','“This time it wasn’t you.','A few minutes later,','Samer returned.','He was holding the container.','He raised it above his head.','“It’s here.','Adam laughed.','“Now you’re the one with a problem keeping track of your belongings.','Samer said:','“It happened once.','Adam replied:','“Everything starts with once.'];
bilMataamPageTranslations[7] = bilMataamClauseTranslations[7].join(' ');
bilMataamClauseTranslations[8] = ['Adam and Yusuf took the same shared taxi,','because their homes were close to each other.','Samer headed in another direction.','Before leaving,','he raised the food container and said:','“Tomorrow’s lunch is ready.','Adam said:','“If you don’t forget it in the shared taxi.','Samer gave him a look,','and walked away.','Adam sat beside the window.','Yusuf sat beside him.','The shared taxi moved off.','A few minutes later,','Yusuf said:','“The restaurant was good.','Adam nodded.','The food was delicious.','The place was stylish.','And the service,','although slow and mistaken about both the platter and the bill,','was good in the end.','He said:','“Yes,','but next time we’ll order less.','Yusuf laughed.','“Don’t take Samer with you.','Adam said:','“He’s the one who showed us the place.','Then he thought for a moment.','“But maybe we can bring him after we order.','They laughed.','The streets were crowded,','but Adam was not in a hurry.','Tomorrow was Friday.','There was no work.','And his family knew he had gone out for dinner.','He messaged his mother:','“I’m on my way home.','A minute later,','she replied:','“Did you eat?','Adam looked at the message.','He was returning from a restaurant,','and had already told her he was going to a restaurant.','Even so,','her first question was:','Did you eat?','He smiled.','He wrote:','“Yes, Mom,','I ate.','She replied:','“Good.','Yusuf looked at Adam’s phone.','He asked:','“Your mother?','Adam nodded.','Yusuf laughed.','“My mother sent me the same question.','The three friends had left three different homes.','They had eaten until they were full.','And paid a restaurant bill.','Even so,','their mothers still wanted to make sure they had eaten.','Adam thought that some things never change.'];
bilMataamPageTranslations[8] = bilMataamClauseTranslations[8].join(' ');

bilMataamClauseTranslations[9] = ['When Adam reached home,','his father was sitting in the living room and Nour was holding her phone.','As soon as he entered,','Nour asked:','“How was the restaurant?','Adam took off his jacket.','He said:','“Good.','Nour said:','“Just good?','Adam looked at her.','“What do you want me to say?','She said she had seen pictures of the restaurant,','and everyone praised it.','Adam sat on the sofa.','He began telling them the story.','The waiting.','Samer and the menu.','The wrong platter.','The extra fries.','The incorrect bill.','And the food container Samer left on the shop window.','Nour laughed.','She said:','“Can’t you go anywhere without something happening to you?','Adam thought about it.','True.','Almost every outing with Samer and Yusuf included some incident.','But those were the things that made the outing worth retelling afterward.','His father asked about the price.','Adam told him how much he had paid.','His father raised his eyebrows.','“For what?','Adam began listing the food.','His father said:','“For that amount, your mother could cook enough food for two days.','From the kitchen,','his mother’s voice came:','“Not two days.','Longer.','Adam laughed.','He had known this discussion would happen.','Nour asked:','“Would you go there again?','Adam was silent for a moment.','Then he said:','“Yes.','Even though they had waited.','Even though the order was delayed.','And even though the bill contained a mistake.','The food was delicious.','The company was enjoyable.','And they had laughed a lot.','Nour said:','“So what would you give it out of ten?','Adam considered it as though the question were extremely serious.','“Seven and a half.','Nour said:','“Why the half?','Adam replied:','“Because of the fries.','Nour did not understand.','Adam laughed.','He did not explain.','He entered his room.','He changed his clothes,','and opened his phone.','There was a message from Samer in the group chat.','A picture of the food container on the table at his home.','Under it:','“It arrived safely.','Yusuf replied:','“Be careful not to forget it in the refrigerator.','Adam sent:','“Next time, I’m ordering.','Samer immediately replied:','“No.','Adam laughed.','He put the phone aside.','The restaurant was good.','But as with every enjoyable outing,','the place was not the most important thing.','What mattered most was who sat at the table.','Who ate half the fries before the food arrived.','Who noticed the error on the bill.','And whom they would keep reminding of this dinner whenever one of them ordered too much food.','Adam turned off the light.','Before falling asleep,','he thought of one sentence:','Next time… nobody should let Samer hold the menu.',''];
bilMataamPageTranslations[9] = bilMataamClauseTranslations[9].join(' ');

const siraPageTranslations = Array(24).fill('');
const siraClauseTranslations = Array(24).fill(null);
siraClauseTranslations[0] = ['Mecca was surrounded by mountains.','Harsh rocky mountains rose around a dry valley,','with no rivers running through it,','and none of the green farmland known in parts of Greater Syria and Yemen.','Even so,','Mecca was not a forgotten city in the desert.','The caravans knew it.','The merchants knew it.','And the Arab tribes knew the road leading to it.','For in the middle of that valley,','stood an ancient House of immense importance to the Arabs:','The Kaaba.','The Arabs made pilgrimage to it,','circled around it,','and recognized it as a sacred House.','The origin of this House was connected to Abraham and Ishmael, peace be upon them.','They raised its foundations while praying to God:','“Our Lord, accept this from us. You are indeed the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.” The message was clear:','God alone was to be worshiped.','But centuries passed.','People changed.','Idols gradually entered their lives,','until they became part of the religion of many Arabs.','Idols came to be placed around the Kaaba.','Silent stones.','They could not hear.','They could not see.','They possessed no power to benefit or harm even themselves.','Yet,','people sought their favor, sacrificed before them, and asked them for help.','Idolatry was not the only problem.','Arab society contained deep contradictions.','There was generosity,','courage,','loyalty,','and protection of one’s neighbors and guests.','But there were also long wars,','tribal fanaticism,','injustice,','and the denial of the weak person’s rights.','A war between two tribes might begin over something small,','then be inherited by sons from their fathers,','and continue for years.','The tribe was the fortress that protected a person.','Whoever belonged to a powerful tribe,','found people to defend him.','But whoever was weak and had no one to support him,','was more vulnerable to oppression.','At the heart of this world stood Quraysh.','Quraysh was no ordinary tribe in the eyes of the Arabs.','It was the tribe of Mecca,','the people of the Sacred Precinct,','and some of its men managed the affairs of the Kaaba and served the pilgrims.','It also held an important commercial position.','Its caravans traveled to Yemen in winter,','and to Greater Syria in summer.','They carried goods.','And returned with others.','News, stories, and accounts of distant lands traveled with them.','Quraysh contained many clans and households.','Among the noblest were Banu Hashim.','Among Banu Hashim was a man of great standing in Mecca.','Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim.','His name was well known among the people of Mecca.','He possessed dignity and standing among his people.','Among his sons was a young man named:','Abdullah.','The people of Mecca did not know that this young man would father someone whose message would transform the Arabian Peninsula,','then reach beyond its borders to every part of the earth.','Abdullah married Amina bint Wahb.','Amina belonged to Banu Zuhra,','one of the clans of Quraysh.','The married couple began their life together.','But it did not last long.','Amina became pregnant,','carrying the child who would later be named Muhammad.','During her pregnancy,','Abdullah left on a journey.','Travel was not unusual for the men of Quraysh.','Trade and caravans were part of their lives.','Abdullah departed.','But he never returned home.','On his way back,','he fell ill and remained in Yathrib.','Then the news reached Mecca:','Abdullah had died.','His son had not yet been born.','Before Muhammad ﷺ opened his eyes to the world,','he had already lost his father.','He would never remember his voice.','He would never remember his face.','He would have no single memory of being with him.','He would be born fatherless.','And Amina awaited his birth alone.','During that period,','a momentous event occurred that the Arabs would remember for a long time.','In Yemen lived a man named Abraha.','He wanted to turn the Arabs away from the Kaaba.','Then he marched toward Mecca with an army to destroy it.','The army had an elephant, or perhaps several elephants.','To the Arabs,','the sight of an army accompanied by an elephant was terrifying.','Mecca was not a fortified city protected by a mighty army.','Quraysh possessed no force equal to that army.','The danger drew close to the Sacred House.','Abd al-Muttalib was then one of the leaders of Quraysh.','In the end, the people of Mecca withdrew rather than confront the army.','There was no vast Meccan army capable of stopping Abraha.','The road before him appeared open.','But Abraha did not destroy the Kaaba.','God protected His House.','The Quran later described what occurred:','“Have you not seen how your Lord dealt with the army of the elephant? Did He not cause their plan to fail? He sent against them flocks of birds, pelting them with stones of baked clay, leaving them like chewed-up straw.” The Kaaba remained standing.','That year became known among the Arabs as:','The Year of the Elephant.','And in that year Muhammad ﷺ was born.','In Mecca,','Amina bint Wahb gave birth to her child.','His father was not there to hold him.','Abdullah had died before seeing his son.','But his grandfather, Abd al-Muttalib, was present.','The child was named:','Muhammad.','Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib.','From Quraysh.','From Banu Hashim.','He was born without a living father.','Mecca did not know what awaited this child.','At that moment,','there was no Islamic state.','There were no Muslims.','The Quran had not yet been revealed.','And Muhammad ﷺ did not yet know that he would become a prophet.','He was only a small child.','Carried in the arms of his family.','Outside,','Mecca continued living as it always had.','Merchants bought and sold.','Caravans departed and returned.','Tribes competed with one another.','And idols still surrounded the Kaaba.','No one knew that years later this small child would stand in that same city,','and call his people to one declaration:','There is no god worthy of worship except God.','That declaration would divide even those closest to him.','Some would believe in him.','Some would be tortured because of him.','Some would be driven from their homes.','And some would take up the sword to fight him.','A day would come when this child, born in Mecca, would be forced to leave it as an emigrant.','Then he would return years later.','On one of the greatest days in its history.','But all of that was still far away.','For Muhammad ﷺ was now.','Still a child.','The next step in his life would take him far from the homes and mountains of Mecca.','Into the desert.','And to a woman from Banu Saad whose name would remain connected to his childhood ﷺ:','Halima al-Saadiyya.',''];
siraPageTranslations[0] = siraClauseTranslations[0].join(' ');
siraClauseTranslations[1] = ['It was customary for some families in Mecca to send their children into the desert to spend their earliest years there.','Women from the desert would come to Mecca seeking children to nurse and care for.','Among these women was one from Banu Saad.','Her name was:','Halima al-Saadiyya.','The child Muhammad ﷺ had no living father.','There was no father behind him who would return from trade and generously reward the woman who nursed his son.','Yet Halima took him with her.','Muhammad ﷺ left Mecca at the beginning of his life.','He left its homes, the Kaaba, and the nearby mountains,','and went to the desert lands of Banu Saad.','There he spent several years of his childhood.','He grew up far from the noise of Mecca.','Wide-open land.','An open sky.','And a simple desert life.','Halima and her family witnessed blessings that made them deeply attached to this child.','Halima loved and cared for him.','Then an extraordinary event, reliably reported in the Sunnah, occurred during his childhood.','The opening of the chest.','Gabriel, peace be upon him, came to him,','opened his chest,','removed his heart and purified it.','Muhammad ﷺ was still young.','He did not yet know what awaited him.','After spending those years among Banu Saad,','he returned to his mother.','To Amina.','But the child who had been born without a father,','was about to face another loss.'];
siraPageTranslations[1] = siraClauseTranslations[1].join(' ');

siraClauseTranslations[2] = ['Muhammad ﷺ lived with his mother Amina.','At about six years of age,','she took him toward Yathrib.','Yathrib was the city that the world would later know as:','The Prophet’s City—Medina.','But Muhammad ﷺ did not enter it this time as a prophet and emigrant.','He entered as a child with his mother.','Then the journey back to Mecca began.','On the way,','Amina fell ill.','At a place called al-Abwa,','his mother died.','Muhammad ﷺ was about six years old.','He had lost his father before ever seeing him.','Now he had lost his mother too.','The child returned to Mecca without her.','He had become an orphan of both parents.','His grandfather, Abd al-Muttalib, took responsibility for him.','He loved him and kept him close.','But the days did not spare the child for long.','About two years later,','Abd al-Muttalib died.','Muhammad ﷺ was around eight years old.','A father lost before birth.','A mother at six.','And a grandfather at eight.','His care then passed to his uncle:','Abu Talib.','Abu Talib would remain beside his nephew for many years.','He would see him as a child.','Then as a young man.','Then as a husband.','Then a day would come when Muhammad ﷺ would stand before Quraysh and declare that he was God’s Messenger.','At that point,','everything would change.'];
siraPageTranslations[2] = siraClauseTranslations[2].join(' ');

siraClauseTranslations[3] = ['The years passed.','Muhammad ﷺ grew up.','He was not raised in a palace.','Nor did he live the life of kings.','In his youth he tended sheep,','then worked in trade.','In a society filled with rivalry and conflict,','Muhammad ﷺ became known for his honesty and trustworthiness.','He was not among those who worshiped idols.','In Mecca lived a noble and wealthy woman named:','Khadija bint Khuwaylid, may God be pleased with her.','She employed men to conduct her trade.','Muhammad ﷺ worked in her business.','Then he married her.','He was twenty-five years old.','Thus began a household that would play a vital role during the earliest years of his mission.','Muhammad ﷺ and Khadija were blessed with children,','and he lived as a husband and father.','The years passed.','Several years before his prophethood,','Quraysh rebuilt the Kaaba.','When they reached the place of the Black Stone,','they disagreed.','Who would put it back in its place?','Every tribe wanted that honor.','The dispute nearly turned into fighting.','Then they agreed that the first person to enter would arbitrate between them.','That person was Muhammad ﷺ.','The Stone was placed on a cloth,','the tribes shared in lifting it,','then Muhammad ﷺ placed it in position.','The crisis ended.','Bloodshed was prevented.','Mecca knew Muhammad ﷺ.','And trusted him.','Yet that same city would turn against him only a few years later.'];
siraPageTranslations[3] = siraClauseTranslations[3].join(' ');
siraClauseTranslations[4] = ['Muhammad ﷺ was approaching the age of forty.','He began to love solitude.','He would leave Mecca and climb to the Cave of Hira.','Away from the noise of the market.','Away from the idols.','Away from people’s daily life.','There he worshiped.','Then came a night after which the world would never be the same.','Muhammad ﷺ was in the cave.','The angel came to him.','Gabriel, peace be upon him.','And said to him:','“Read.” He replied:','“I cannot read.” Then the first words of the Quran were revealed:','“Read in the name of your Lord who created; created humankind from a clinging form. Read, and your Lord is the Most Generous; who taught by the pen; taught humanity what it did not know.” Muhammad ﷺ left the cave and returned to Khadija.','His heart trembled from the enormity of what he had witnessed.','He said:','“Cover me, cover me.” Khadija covered him until his fear subsided.','Then he told her what had happened.','Khadija was the first person to stand beside him.','She reminded him of his virtues: maintaining family ties,','supporting those burdened by hardship,','and helping people through just causes and calamities.','Then she took him to Waraqa ibn Nawfal.','When Waraqa heard what had happened,','he recognized that the one who had come to Muhammad was the same angel who had come to the prophets before him.','Muhammad ibn Abdullah ﷺ had entered the cave as a man from Mecca.','He emerged from it,','a prophet.',''];
siraPageTranslations[4] = siraClauseTranslations[4].join(' ');

siraClauseTranslations[5] = ['Khadija, may God be pleased with her, believed.','Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, believed.','Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, believed while still a boy.','Zayd ibn Haritha, may God be pleased with him, believed.','The number of Muslims began to grow.','At first,','the call remained within a limited circle.','Then came the command to proclaim it openly.','At this point the confrontation began.','Muhammad’s ﷺ message was not merely a call to good character.','It declared:','Worship God alone.','This meant that the idols worshiped by Quraysh and their ancestors did not deserve worship.','Quraysh began to see the call as a threat.','They tried to stop it.','But Muhammad ﷺ did not stop.','When they could not silence him,','they turned against those who believed in him.','Especially the vulnerable who had no powerful tribes to protect them.','Among them was Bilal ibn Rabah, may God be pleased with him.','He was tortured in the heat of Mecca so that he would abandon his faith.','But he remained steadfast.','He would say:','“One,','One.” The family of Yasir was also tortured.','Sumayya, may God be pleased with her, was killed.','For a person to say:','“I believe in Muhammad” had become a decision that could cost wealth, security, and life.','Even so,','the number of Muslims continued to grow.'];
siraPageTranslations[5] = siraClauseTranslations[5].join(' ');

siraClauseTranslations[6] = ['The persecution intensified.','Some Muslims could no longer live safely in Mecca.','The Prophet ﷺ permitted some of them to migrate to Abyssinia.','This was a difficult decision.','To leave Mecca.','One’s home.','One’s family.','One’s homeland.','And cross the sea to an unfamiliar country.','But Abyssinia had a just king: the Negus.','The emigrants arrived.','Then Quraysh sent representatives who tried to bring them back.','Jafar ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, stood before the Negus and explained what Islam had brought.','He recited to him from Surah Maryam.','The Negus did not hand the Muslims over to Quraysh.','Abyssinia became a refuge for a number of believers.','As for the Prophet ﷺ,','he remained in Mecca.'];
siraPageTranslations[6] = siraClauseTranslations[6].join(' ');

siraClauseTranslations[7] = ['Quraysh failed to stop the call.','So they made a harsh decision.','They would boycott Banu Hashim and everyone who protected Muhammad ﷺ.','No selling to them.','No buying from them.','No marriage with them.','And no dealings with them.','The siege grew severe.','Difficult years passed.','Eventually the boycott ended.','But the relief did not last.','Two people had provided the Prophet ﷺ with immense support.','Abu Talib.','His uncle, who protected him from Quraysh.','And Khadija, may God be pleased with her.','His wife, who believed in him from the very first moment.','Within a short period,','he lost them both.','Abu Talib died.','Then Khadija, may God be pleased with her, died.','His grief was profound.','And the Prophet’s ﷺ position in Mecca became even more difficult.'];
siraPageTranslations[7] = siraClauseTranslations[7].join(' ');

